sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Turing k_c at 104 µm on Eusthenopteron foordi, with sweep, ablation, and specimen GOF — MorphoEval overall 86.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg system (a=0.1, b=0.9, Dv/Du=12, λ_formula=104.2 µm, age 379 Ma, chronoseries 1/1). Dispersion Pearson r=0.9999998, RMSE=0.00261 on the real-eigenvalue band. Realized wavelength 102.01 µm. Equal-diffusion std=1.69e-6 versus pattern std=0.483. Autocatalysis ablation std is numerically zero. Dv/Du sweep Spearman r=0.90 (not strictly monotone: 111.57, 110.65, 111.84 µm at ratios 12, 16, 22). Fossil mask aspect 3.62 versus gallery reconstruction 3.91. Orientation KS=0.024. GIF is 10 frames at 974×480. Signing was unavailable. Overall 86.1/100 (faithfulness 85.3, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/eusthenopteron_foordi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 631334 B, 1584×888 px, artifact_sha256 721d8d4672825d003f90b6fdfb105ec4274bfb531a752756f483adad178cf1c5 (sha256 721d8d4672825d003f90b6fdfb105ec4274bfb531a752756f483adad178cf1c5), spec_fingerprint 7d5c5c4a83fa8f6c063e1e197796aa4e97931ea29ced33c300363ee59ac62e99. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7d5c5c4a83fa8f6c063e1e197796aa4e97931ea29ced33c300363ee59ac62e99; artifact_sha256: 721d8d4672825d003f90b6fdfb105ec4274bfb531a752756f483adad178cf1c5. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-eusthenopteron-foordi-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and diffusion-driven instability | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Kondo and Asai 1995 and Nakamasu et al. 2009 pigment-cell RD on living fish | Andrews and Westoll 1970 skeleton of Eusthenopteron foordi; reconstructed_in_script: Parameters chosen so formula k_c equals 2π per 104.2 µm | Dispersion comparison, Dv/Du sweep, equal-diffusion control, autocatalysis ablation | Body mask from the Brussels photograph used as the display domain; transfer_boundary: Living-teleost chromatophore RD transferred onto a Frasnian tristichopterid | 104.2 µm is the assigned primordium-tier detail scale; does_not_claim: That orange ocelli are preserved on the fossil | That the photograph has a micrometre scale bar | That the successor mode-count uses a newly measured body length rather than the registry lengths 0.140 m and 0.165 m." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Dv/Du wavelength sweep is rank-correlated (Spearman 0.90) but not strictly monotone; the ratio-10 run is only weakly patterned.",
            "remediation needed: Still one fossil photograph and one builder-assessor. A second assessor and a scale-barred specimen would be the next gain." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.861"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

